1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,790
You're way too arrogant, Leo.

3
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,260
The Captain already made himself perfectly clear.

4
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,700
Enough with the chatter.

5
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:34,620
So the Captain's plan means nothing to you?

6
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,500
And you just blow off the Coach too?

7
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:38,940
Don't be so upset.

8
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,300
He probably didn't mean anything by it.

9
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:45,150
If this really was one of our own Players,

10
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,400
I will make sure there are severe consequences.

11
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,910
No mercy. They'll be kicked off the Team.

12
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,350
I'm handling this seriously,

13
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:54,300
Leo, You want to explain yourself?

14
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,520
I didn't steal the Cheese,
so I've got nothing to say.

15
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:59,100
Leo.

16
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:00,540
What kind of attitude is that?

17
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:06,000
Episode 19

18
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:08,700
I think this time back home,

19
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:11,280
It'll probably be really helpful for my future.

20
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:14,460
But for now,

21
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,380
I've gotta go.

22
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:19,740
You're really leaving?

23
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:25,980
Leo... we don't want you to go.

24
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:27,000
Exactly.

25
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,420
You can always go back to America later,

26
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,460
after you've gotten more out of this.

27
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:37,020
Meeting all of you has already been
more than I could've asked for.

28
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,300
Alright, you guys head back now.
No need to see me off.

29
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,780
Come on, just a little further.

30
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,900
Alright, morning Practice is about to start.

31
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,820
You should get back. Don't be late.

32
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,700
Bye.

33
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,020
Sis, we should head back.

34
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,500
Beautiful encounters rarely have a happy ending.

35
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,460
To crush this Exhibition Match

36
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,860
and show everyone what the Jianghai Team is made of,

37
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:56,220
every Team member must use every single
second to train at full capacity.

38
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:57,660
Give it everything you've got.

39
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:00,490
We need to perfect our Signature Moves as fast as possible.

40
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,420
No distractions allowed!

41
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,860
All your energy goes into Training.

42
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,740
The specific Training Plan

43
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:10,620
will strictly follow the schedule I already laid out.

44
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:15,900
Training starts now!

45
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Hey!

46
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,900
So these are the Legendary
Jianghai Team Signature Moves?

47
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,300
Stop being a smart ass, Hugo.

48
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,660
To beat a Player at your level,
I don't even need my Signature Moves.

49
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,580
You're all talk.

50
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,500
The Match hasn't even begun.

51
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:04,380
Don't you think you're bragging a little too early?

52
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,780
I knew you'd be this cocky,

53
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:10,140
so I made sure to take this
path today just to run into you.

54
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,060
What, you looking for a fight or something?

55
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:15,900
A fight? Sorry, I'm not in the mood for that today.

56
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,780
So you're saying you want a Yo-Yo battle?

57
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,180
Exactly. That's what I was hoping you'd say.

58
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:24,540
Captain, you're gonna step in and duel him?

59
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:27,420
Isn't that a bit like using a sledgehammer to swat a fly?

60
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,340
What a waste of time.

61
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,740
It's no big deal.

62
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,620
Think of it as a warm-up for the Exhibition Match.

63
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:36,540
What a coincidence.

64
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,900
I was just thinking I'd knock you guys down a
peg or two before the real thing.

65
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:36,540
Phantom Shockwave!

66
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,460
Spiral Wind Wave!

67
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:11,330
Hmph! Our Captain hasn't even
started using his real tricks yet.

68
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:12,540
No need.

69
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:13,980
You've got blind courage, I'll give you that.

70
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,900
Take some time to think about that. Let's go.

71
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,700
Let's just pretend this never happened.

72
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:01,500
Welcome! Hello!

73
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,780
Principal Qian! Principal Qian!

74
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,700
Good, good. Very good.

75
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,620
You've all worked so hard!

76
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,060
Monica, I've missed you so much!

77
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:13,980
Son, look who's here!

78
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,860
Dad! I didn't think you were actually coming.

79
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,780
I was just messing with you.

80
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,700
Dad wanted to surprise you.

81
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,020
Mickey, what exactly did you tell him on the phone?

82
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:27,420
Oh, come on. I already sorted it out with Dad.

83
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:29,820
He said he'd definitely come watch us compete.

84
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,740
So why don't I see him anywhere?

85
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,100
He's probably stuck in some negotiation or something.

86
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,180
Dad!

87
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,540
Dad! What took you so long?

88
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,940
Better late than never, right?

89
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:52,860
Your Old Man's here to cheer you on!

90
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:54,780
Yeah! Awesome!

91
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:56,000
Lets go!

92
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:57,250
Do your best out there!

93
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,460
You messed up the knot again. Seriously.

94
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,840
If you don't have the skills,
don't try to do a job this delicate.

95
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:09,150
Well, Manager Ma is out of town,

96
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,140
and he asked me to fill in.

97
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:11,580
I couldn't say no.

98
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,980
Couldn't say no? You just didn't try hard enough.

99
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,380
You think being a Host is easy?

100
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,700
Manager Ma said my Mandarin is the best.

101
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,100
I'm a perfect fit for the job.

102
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,770
Anyone can tell where you're from just by listening.

103
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:28,880
You call that Mandarin?

104
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,740
Oh man, how could you forget?

105
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:35,180
Back in our village, I was the guy on the loudspeaker.

106
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,820
Almost got it...

107
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,260
Let me, let me, I got this.

108
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,180
Hey, you're doing it wrong.

109
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,300
That's not how it goes.

110
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,180
I'm just gonna find someone else to help.

111
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:09,180
Come on, come on. Coach Tony! Come here!

112
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,000
Coach Tony,

113
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,430
You've had the kids out here Training for so long.

114
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,420
You've all worked hard.

115
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,820
It's scorching out here and I can't really do much to help,

116
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,740
so I just brought you guys some cold drinks.

117
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,660
Everyone cool down and beat the heat!

118
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:24,540
Oh, you really shouldn't have!

119
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:25,950
Please, don't be so polite.

120
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,670
It's just a small gesture from a Parent.

121
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:30,300
We appreciate the gesture.

122
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,700
But I still need to run this by the Principal.

123
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:35,100
Oh, here comes the Principal!

124
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,020
Coach Tony, I've already given this my approval.

125
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,420
And on behalf of the School,

126
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,340
I'd like to thank Mr. Song for his generosity.

127
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,260
As for this kind gesture, Mr. Song,

128
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:47,580
our School is hardly worthy of it,
but we couldn't possibly refuse.

129
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,940
Yes, yes. The Principal is absolutely right.

130
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:53,340
Then we'll just say thank you very much!

131
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,460
Don't mention it. Thank *you*!

132
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,620
Shawn!

133
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:01,500
Coach, Shawn has wandered off somewhere.
I couldn't find him.

134
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,860
You see what I mean about my Logistics Manager?

135
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,780
He's never around when you need him.

136
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,670
Alright, how about this. Mark!

137
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,020
Grab a few guys and unload the drinks.

138
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,580
No, no, that won't be necessary.

139
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,740
They've got a match to focus on.

140
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:14,910
Dad, come on!

141
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,260
The Match is about to start.

142
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:20,220
I'm up first! Let's go, hurry up!

143
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,180
We're going, we're going.

144
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:23,550
I'll head over there first then.

145
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:24,540
Man, you're in a rush.

146
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,390
Everyone!

147
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:07,260
Everyone, settle down!

148
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:11,580
Today is the Friendly Yo-Yo Exhibition Match

149
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:14,460
between Jianghai Team and Chengnan Team!

150
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,340
I'm honored that you all thought of me

151
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:19,260
to be your Host.

152
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:24,540
I feel about 120,000% honored.

153
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:33,260
On behalf of the Leadership here at Falcon Base,

154
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:36,540
I'd like to welcome you all here today.

155
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:49,020
Ever since our two Teams arrived at Falcon Base,

156
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:53,420
the whole place has been buzzing with life and energy.

157
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,740
These kids...

158
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:59,100
Each and every one of them is so pure, so cute.

159
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:00,730
They're hardworking,

160
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:03,900
they're clever,

161
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,780
and they've got both courage and brains.

162
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,220
You sure know a lot of fancy words.

163
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,500
To put it in a way a Chef like me would explain—

164
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:14,580
it's like having a full kitchen:
You can fry, sauté, broil, and grill.

165
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,380
Enough with the chatter, let's get this started!

166
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:18,780
Alright, alright!

167
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:23,100
I'll now read aloud the rules for today's Match.

168
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:30,780
Today's competition will use a King of the Hill format.

169
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:35,100
Each Team will first send one Player to the stage.

170
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:38,460
The winner stays on to defend the hill,

171
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:43,260
and the losing Team can send
up another Player to Challenge.

172
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,100
No Player is allowed to compete twice.

173
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:52,860
This continues until one Team runs out of Challengers.

174
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:57,050
At that point, the Team left standing wins the Match.

175
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,060
Everyone got it?

176
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,380
Now, the Match officially begins!

177
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:28,380
Go Chengnan! Go!

178
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:31,940
That's my boy!

179
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:36,060
Chengnan's got this!

180
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:37,020
Chengnan!

181
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:17,340
Yeah!

182
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,420
Jianghai takes the Hill!

183
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,340
My boy won!

184
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,100
Jianghai's got this!

185
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,780
Go, Chuck!

186
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,900
Look, look! That's my Son!

187
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,580
Jianghai successfully defends their Hill!

188
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,900
My boy won again!

189
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:42,780
Do you have to be so extra?

190
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,220
Of course, I totally do!

191
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:46,140
Because of you, Its all spilled onto me.

192
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:50,940
Oh no, I'm so sorry!

193
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,260
Let me wipe it for you.

194
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,680
Don't worry about it.

195
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,470
Go, Chuck!

196
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:03,900
Good. I knew it all along.

197
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:05,960
The strength of the Jianghai Team is no joke.

198
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:09,660
Back in the day, we had zero funding

199
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,100
and no proper place to Train.

200
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,020
But I still managed to pull this Team together.

201
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,900
It was tough. Really tough.

202
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:19,740
We had to get results without
letting it affect their schoolwork.

203
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:23,100
Believe me, I've been through the ringer.

204
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,940
Yeah, you're telling me.

205
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:35,100
Jianghai's got this!

206
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:37,100
Jianghai's got this!

207
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:52,860
Go, Son!

208
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:54,780
Jianghai's got this!

209
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,700
Go, Chuck!

210
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,140
Jianghai's got this!

211
00:19:58,500 --> 00:19:59,500
Go, Chuck!

212
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:01,980
Jianghai's got this!

213
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,220
Yeah!

214
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,900
Yes! That was awesome!

215
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:28,860
Way to go, Chuck!

216
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,750
Nice one! Go!

217
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:35,580
Nice job!

218
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:47,580
Chengnan takes the hill!

219
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:51,900
Chengnan's got this!

220
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:53,340
Go, Zoe!

221
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,230
Chengnan's got this!

222
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:56,700
Go, Zoe!

223
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:57,660
Let's go!

224
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:04,430
It's okay. You'll get 'em next time.

225
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,440
Monica, you're up!

226
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:12,030
Go! Go, Monica! Go!

227
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:12,540
Go, Monica! Go!

228
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,380
Jianghai's got this!

229
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:20,220
Jianghai's got this!

230
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:25,580
Go, Chengnan!

